  "title": "Why is debugging distributed, complex production systems still this hard?",
  "description": "Azure native applications built on AKS produce logs, metrics, and traces across highly distributed systems. During an incident, correlating that data across services, dependencies, and recent changes becomes the hardest part of the problem. This discussion focuses on how developers approach that challenge today and how it can be improved.\n\nSeating for this session is first-come, first-served. Add it to your schedule to plan your day and arrive early to secure a spot.",
